INT. FREIGHT ELEVATOR, SHUTTERED TEXTILE MILL - NIGHT

A steel cage the size of a small room. Dim bulb. A brass gate. Dust.

A MAN IN A LEATHER JACKET (40s, scar through his lip) leans against the back wall. A smoking pistol hangs loose in his fist.

The gate rattles. A hand grips it from outside.

A WOMAN (30s, long coat, blood on her cuff) slides in, pulls the gate shut, and presses the lever. The elevator lurches down.

They face each other. Silence, except for the cables.

WOMAN
You're late.

MAN
You're early.

WOMAN
I was told midnight.

MAN
Midnight was the plan.

She looks at his pistol. He tucks it slowly into his waistband.

WOMAN
Where's the third?

MAN
Dead.

WOMAN
How?

MAN
Quickly.

The cable groans. The bulb flickers. She steps close and he flinches, then stills.

She reaches into his jacket, withdraws a leather folio, flips it open. A set of blueprints. A passport. A photograph.

WOMAN (CONT'D)
(reading)
Matteo Ferrante.

MAN
That's me.

WOMAN
It isn't.

MAN
It is tonight.

WOMAN
(low)
Tell me your real name.

MAN
Why?

WOMAN
So I know whom to shoot.

He grins, tilts his head. The elevator thumps to a halt between floors. The lights die. Total dark.

In the dark, a scuffle. A thud. A gasp. A pistol clatters on the floor. Someone lunges, someone slams a wall, a body falls against the gate and it rattles open. The bulb sputters back to life.

The woman has the man pinned against the cage, forearm across his throat. His hands are on her wrists. Both breathing hard. The pistol lies between their feet.

MAN (CONT'D)
(strained)
Stefan.

WOMAN
Stefan what?

STEFAN
Stefan Halloran.

WOMAN
(releasing him)
My brother.

STEFAN
Naomi.

NAOMI
You're alive.

STEFAN
Barely.

She slaps him, hard. Then hugs him, fiercer than a boxer.

NAOMI (CONT'D)
Twelve years.

STEFAN
Eleven and a half.

NAOMI
I'm still going to kill you.

STEFAN
Do it after we get out.

The elevator groans. Starts to move again, down, into the dark.
